dwi-dmipy ports the NODDI-Watson model and brute2fine procedure from
AthenaEPI/dmipy commit 2d6073218eb4ebc97645ac6e275270c36834e33d (1.0.5).
Copyright (c) 2017 Rutger Fick & Demian Wassermann. MIT; see LICENSE-DMIPY.
source.manifest.json identifies every consulted source file by SHA-256.

src/sampling.rs contains the source's 30 starting directions and the 362
hemisphere vertices from DIPY1.7.0's symmetric724 sphere. The DIPY-derived
vertices retain DIPY's BSD-3-Clause terms; see LICENSE-DIPY.

The L-BFGS-B implementation is reused from dwi-gp, whose source and notices
identify its SciPy/L-BFGS-B BSD-3-Clause and MIT origins. This crate does not
copy SciPy's Fortran optimizer or the unlicensed NODDI toolbox erfi function.

The hyp1f1(1/2,3/2,kappa) normalizer is evaluated by its convergent positive
power series. No AMICO implementation supplies expected values in the tests.
